  "concept_key": "selection.lexicon.adr",
  "title": "ADR% in 15 seconds",
  "hook": "Why do some stocks need a wider stop?",
  "takeaway": "ADR% (average daily range) is how far a stock moves from low to high on a normal day, averaged over 20 days. In December 2019, Coca-Cola's was 0.9% and Tesla's 2.9%: a 2% stop was never reached by a Coca-Cola day, but 15 of 20 Tesla days moved that much. A stop tighter than one normal day gets hit by noise.",
  "learn": [
    "ADR% is how far a stock moves from its low to its high on a normal day, averaged over 20 days.",
    "In December 2019, Coca-Cola's ADR was 0.9% and Tesla's was 2.9%.",
    "A 2% stop was never reached by a Coca-Cola day but was reached on 15 of 20 Tesla days, so a stop tighter than a normal day gets hit by noise."
  ],
  "glossary": {
    "ADR": "how far a stock moves, low to high, on a normal day"
  },
